WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Use a consistent identity model across local services, cloud accounts, gateways, storage,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:05.920
and applications.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.640
Grant least privilege and require authentication at every exposed endpoint.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.815
Segment management, model-serving, storage,

00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:15.950
and user traffic so compromise of a front end does not provide unrestricted access to

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.675
private data or infrastructure.

00:00:17.675 --> 00:00:21.995
Store provider keys, model tokens, and service credentials in managed secrets systems.

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:25.895
Rotate them, restrict their scope, and prevent them from entering prompts, images,

00:00:25.895 --> 00:00:27.375
repositories, or logs.

00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:31.735
Patch local operating systems, GPU drivers, runtimes, gateways, containers,

00:00:31.735 --> 00:00:33.810
and cloud components through controlled releases.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:38.355
Hybrid systems have a larger dependency surface, so version inventory and rollback matter.

00:00:38.355 --> 00:00:42.960
Audit routing decisions, configuration changes, authentication, administrative actions,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.040
costs, errors, and security events.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.205
Minimize sensitive prompt and output content in logs while preserving enough evidence to

00:00:49.205 --> 00:00:50.311
investigate incidents.

00:00:50.311 --> 00:00:54.690
Correlate local and cloud timestamps and request identifiers so an end-to-end event can be

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.440
reconstructed without copying private data into every monitoring system.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.055
Prepare incident procedures for data misrouting, exposed credentials, provider outage,

00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:05.360
compromised local nodes, and unexpected spending.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.620
Define how to disable a route, revoke keys, isolate systems, preserve evidence,

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.375
restore configuration, and communicate degraded capability.

00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:15.400
Back up irreplaceable data and policy, and test rollback.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.145
Review vendor security, availability, retention,

00:01:18.145 --> 00:01:21.240
and exit options because provider risk is part of the architecture,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.350
not an external footnote.
